      "q": "18. A spherical mirror and a thin spherical lens have each a focal length of $-15cm$ . The mirror and the lens are likely to be\nBoth concave\nBoth convex\nThe mirror is concave and the lens is convex\nThe mirror is convex, but the lens is concave",
      "a": "a) For a concave lens the primary focus is on the same side as the object and is negative. In the case of a concave mirror, the focus is in front of the mirror and negative. Therefore, the mirror and lens are likely to be concave."
