      "q": "12. Why does the Sun appear reddish early in the morning?",
      "a": "During sunrise, the light rays from the sun travel a greater distance in the earth\u2019s atmosphere before reaching our eyes. In this journey, the shorter wavelengths of lights are spread out and only the longer wavelengths reach our eyes.\nSince blue colour has a short wavelength and red colour has a long wavelength, red colour can reach our eyes after the atmospheric scattering of light. Thus, the sun appears to be reddish early in the morning."
